# Dockerfile.server runs `uv sync` to build /app/server/.venv, then does
# `COPY server/ server/`. Without this, the host's macOS .venv is copied over
# the one uv just built and its bin/python becomes a symlink into
# /Users/.../uv/python/cpython-*-macos-aarch64 — which does not exist in the
# image, so the container dies with "exec: server/.venv/bin/python: not found".
**/.venv
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
.git
*.log
data/
models/
